{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfev63UQiv8jvdb7nGWT7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe `AssignCustomerCode` logic itself lives in the right unit, but two structural/coherence issues:\n\n1. **Duplicated transformation in `AssignCustomerCode.service`.** `city3` and `last3` are now computed with the identical expression `x.substring(0, Math.min(3, x.length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)`. With the change this pattern appears twice verbatim. Extract a small private helper (e.g. `firstThreeUpper(String)`) so both derivations read the same and the \"first three, upper-cased\" rule has a single home.\n\n2. **Stale example in the derived value's Javadoc.** The spec says everything derived from `customerCode` — notably the membership number — must be rebuilt on the new format, and the diff duly updated the openapi example to `TOW-SMI-0007-M26`. But the equivalent example in `Owner.getMembershipNumber()`'s Javadoc (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java:154`) still reads `SMI-0007-M26`, the old format. The membership number concatenates `customerCode`, so the runtime value rebuilds automatically, but leaving the Java doc example on the old format while the openapi example moved to the new one is exactly the kind of incoherence a maintainer trips over. Update the Javadoc example to the new format for consistency."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":22572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"791bb8b1-1b4d-4aea-88b8-e5c76cfb11f5","uuid":"a4e85371-3ed2-4416-b803-8b0a058bb8ce","timestamp":"2026-10-03T07:33:58.290Z","requ